# The world where a claim carries no au:rung — an overlay for the derivation
# test, NOT part of the committed corpus.
#
# ⛔ THIS IS A FAIL-OPEN CONTROL, and it is the reason bindings.rq's rung is
# OPTIONAL. When the rung was mandatory, a claim without one emitted no row,
# so it was in no closure, so a LIVE conflict it is party to held nothing —
# and an order whose closure touches an open conflict dispatched. That is the
# exact negation of RFC-002 §10 mechanism 3, arrived at by deleting a triple
# that no SHACL shape requires and that every branch of ladder-integrity.rq
# is itself keyed on, so no gate could see it either.
#
# Not hypothetical: spec's own Studio corpus keeps 46 of its 69 rungs in a
# separately generated terms.ttl, so a dataset listing corpus.ttl alone drops
# two thirds of its claims out of every closure, silently and green.
#
# The claim below is scoped s-market-b (wo-042's own scope) and made a party
# to INV-05, which is OPEN and which wo-042 does not otherwise touch. With the
# fix, wo-042 gains the obligation AND the hold. Without it, both vanish.
@prefix rfc: <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/rfc#> .
@prefix au:  <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/authoring#> .
@prefix amp: <https://ampere.example/corpus#> .

amp:mkt-quiet-hours a rfc:NormativeStatement ;
    rfc:modality rfc:MUST_NOT ;
    rfc:predicate "The resource MUST NOT bid into the evening ramp during declared quiet hours." ;
    au:discipline amp:d-market ;
    au:scopedBy amp:s-market-b .
    # NO au:rung, NO au:stalledOn — deliberately. Both are what the ladder gate
    # keys on, and their absence is what made this claim invisible.

amp:INV-05 au:party amp:mkt-quiet-hours .
